// 🟡 gated — feature:phase1-nat-semiring-rust-rung-interim-nonblocking — bind #3955 §6 (rust rung emit not rustc-clean on main) — dissolve-on-arrival: flip non_blocking to false when rung1 rust_typecheck passes under V4_PHASE1_NAT_SEMIRING_STRICT=1; until then non_blocking: true (continue-on-error at workflow) while STRICT=1 still logs fail-closed rung receipts; forbidden: silent YAML-only continue-on-error without modeled parity.
// 🟡 tracked-bridge — feature:phase1-nat-semiring-rung-gate-binding-smoke — owner:keen-crab-361 (Ladder/Fixture Manager) — bind node://adhoc-2b191c1e-6b3 ("phase1/nat_semiring rung gate binding-smoke test (mirror M1's v4_workflow_ci_m1_rust_emit_probe_modeled_and_bound_to_ci_yml)") — consumer:src/v3/compiler/tests/integration/v4_workflow_ci_runner_dag_smoke_test.rs new test function asserting ci.dag step_name/script_path/non_blocking/timeout_minutes parity with .github/workflows/ci.yml step block — dissolve-on-arrival: binding_smoke_step_name carries the new test's step name (e.g. "phase1/nat_semiring rung gate model/YAML binding smoke") AND ci.yml runs the new test as a cargo-test step paired with the gate; forbidden: re-emptying binding_smoke_step_name after the test lands. Until the bound work item closes, ci.dag↔ci.yml single-authority for THIS signal is enforced by the four-field parity (step_name / script_path / non_blocking / timeout_minutes) under review checkpoint at PR-time — not by a CI binding test.
data phase1_nat_semiring_rung_gate_ci_live_workflow_signal: CiLiveWorkflowStepSignal = {
  binding_smoke_step_name: ""
  step_name: "phase1/nat_semiring rungs 0-2 gate (dag rust python go)"
  script_path: "scripts/v4-phase1-nat-semiring-rung-gate.sh"
  non_blocking: true
  timeout_minutes: 20
